        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Scanner sweep\n\n**Scanner** steps the radio across a range and stops when something is loud enough. Its wire into the Channel's control port is what makes the decoder follow: the scanner decides the frequency, the channel decodes whatever it lands on.\n\n**Spectrum monitor** watches the same band and names what it recognises, whether or not the scanner stopped there. Use it to find out what lives in a band before you scan it.\n\n**Signal hunt** is the other way round: it walks you towards one transmitter by comparing how strong it is as you turn. It needs a directional antenna and a GPS node to be useful; wire one to its position port.\n\n**Decoder log** keeps every hit from the monitor.\n\nEdit the scanner's range for your local allocation."
          },
